Z||000000||GT-maniac||06-06-2000||05:47 PM||||I'm looking at replacing my plug wires and was wondering if anyone is using the red plug wires that the Fiero store sells ?. Are they just regular plug wires only red or are they a fairly decent performance wire set ? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Uaana||06-06-2000||06:17 PM||||You may hear a lot of diff opinions on this but for me the best bang for the buck was the Accel wires from Summit 60bucks and they are 8.8mm high temp, custom pre cut. so no cutting or fitting. as for the fierostore wires they are ok but not worth the cash in my book.<P>just my 4c||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||06-06-2000||06:37 PM||||Taylor Spiro-Pro wires cost me 32 bucks from Summit, pick your color, including red.  No need to worry about the metal boot guards anymore.  Had mine for 6 years with no problem, almost impossible to break the boots.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||06-06-2000||07:54 PM||||Accel SuperStock 8mm spiral core wires cost me about $40 at O'Reillys and have a very nice glossy finish. Very easy to keep clean. But I've heard good things about the Taylor wires too. I have no idea about the specs on the Fierostore wires other than "they're red".||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||06-06-2000||08:50 PM||||This topic has been covered several times.  See posts at  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002720.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002720.html</A>    There's a photo of the Taylor wires there.  I think they look great and haven't had any problems (had them 6 months) AND the stock aluminium heat shields for the plug ends fit! ||||reg||1
